# liquid-snipe — SPEC

"Companion to PROJECT.md. PROJECT defines what and why; SPEC defines how."
"Clean-room implementation in a new Rust crate sibling to liquid-snipe/. Directory: liquid-snipe-rs/. Workspace binary: liquid-snipe. The POC's research informs the design; no POC code is reused or imported at runtime."

## 1. Architecture

### 1.1 The hot loop

"There is ONE runtime loop. Every other concern is either a background task that feeds it cached values, or a worker task it spawns to absorb tx-submit latency."
"Shape is proven by reference/Solana-Sniper-Bot/src/processor/sniper_bot.rs:464-489."

```
HOT LOOP (one tokio task, blocks only on stream.next().await)

loop {
  let raw = stream.next().await;
  let evt = decode(raw);                          // µs, in-process
  persist_async(evt);                             // crossbeam send

  if let Some(pos) = open_positions.get(&evt.mint) {
    pos.apply(&evt);                              // price from evt
    if let Some(action) = strategy.evaluate_exits(pos, &evt) {
      tokio::spawn(execute_sell(pos, action));    // off hot path
    }
  }

  if evt.is_entry_candidate() {
    let dec = strategy.evaluate_buy(&evt, &enrich, &risk);
    if let Some(plan) = dec.fired() {
      tokio::spawn(execute_buy(plan));            // off hot path
    }
  }
}
```

Source {
  // Hot-swappable.
  options = ["Yellowstone gRPC", "Helius WS fallback", "JSONL replay"]
  shape   = "One sub, 8 program IDs"
}

Workers {
  pool = "tokio::spawn(execute_buy / execute_sell)"
  steps = "build → blockhash inject → SWQOS submit"
}

BackgroundTasks {
  blockhash_refresher
  enrichment_prefetcher    // mint + holders + deployer history, LRU + TTL
  housekeeping             // cleanup, expire enrich
  persistence_writer       // drain WAL → DuckDB
  heartbeat                // X3 / X7 fallback every Nms
  slippage_controller      // consec-failure counter, bumps global bps, resets on success
  config_reloader          // SIGHUP → reload TOML → swap source/SWQOS/strategy for new positions
}

### 1.2 What's NOT on the hot path

NotOnHotPath {
  // concern → (location, why)
  getAccountInfo_for_mint_authorities {
    where = "enrichment task"
    why   = "RPC RTT"
  }
  getTokenLargestAccounts_for_LP_burn_and_top10 {
    where = "enrichment task"
    why   = "RPC RTT"
  }
  getSignaturesForAddress_for_deployer_history {
    where = "enrichment task"
    why   = "RPC RTT"
  }
  getLatestBlockhash {
    where = "blockhash refresher (interval configurable)"
    why   = "RPC RTT"
  }
  getBalance_for_wallet {
    where = "own task on [wallet].balance_refresh_ms cadence (default 1s); cached as AtomicU64. Also refreshed eagerly on every fill confirmation."
    why   = "RPC RTT"
  }
  tx_build_sign_submit {
    where = "execute_buy / execute_sell workers"
    why   = "RPC + SWQOS RTT"
  }
  duckdb_writes {
    where = "persistence task draining a crossbeam::channel"
    why   = "append latency"
  }
  wall_clock_sells {
    where = "heartbeat task"
    why   = "event-driven covers the rest (time, decay fallback)"
  }
}

CachingContract {
  "The hot loop reads only from in-memory state."
  reads = ["open_positions: DashMap", "enrich_cache: DashMap", "blockhash: ArcSwap<Hash>", "wallet_balance: AtomicU64", "daily_pnl: AtomicI64", "slippage_bps: AtomicU16"]
  miss_policy = "Enrichment miss for a strategy field → reject candidate with reason `enrichment-pending`, kick off enrichment for next time."
}

### 1.3 Subscriptions

"One Yellowstone gRPC subscription, commitment = Processed."

```rust
SubscribeRequestFilterTransactions {
    vote: Some(false),
    failed: Some(false),
    account_required: vec![],
    account_include: vec![/* DEX program ids from active config */],
    account_exclude: vec![],
    signature: None,
}
```

Subscription {
  "Single filter delivers entry candidates AND price updates on every mint trading on those programs."
  "Membership in open_positions is the inline check that decides whether a buy/sell tx triggers an exit eval."

  HotSwap {
    "SIGHUP-triggered reload re-reads the config; if the gRPC endpoint or [dexes].enabled changed, the source task drops the current stream and reopens with the new params."
    "In-flight events drain naturally."
  }

  Fallback {
    "Helius logsNotifications per program when gRPC is unavailable."
    "Logs alone don't carry reserves, so on the WS path we pay one getTransaction per candidate."
    "Bounded concurrent fetches: [grpc.fallback_ws].max_inflight (default 32), duplicate-signature suppression, short confirmed-visibility retries (3 × 600ms)."
    "Acceptable as degraded mode, not the default."
  }
}

### 1.4 Async model

AsyncModel {
  runtime = "One Tokio multi-thread runtime"
  hot_task = "Owns the stream and inline decode/decide"
  executor_pool = "tokio::spawn(execute_*), bounded by Semaphore (default 8; configurable)"
  background = "Independent tasks (blockhash, enrichment, housekeeping, persistence, heartbeat, slippage controller, config reloader)"
  per_position_tasks = "NONE"
  shutdown = "Single CancellationToken → drop the stream, drain workers, flush persistence, exit. 30s budget; force after."
}

### 1.5 Processed → Confirmed reconciliation

"Hot loop acts on Processed events. A separate confirmation_audit task re-checks every fill at Confirmed after [confirmation_audit].delay_ms (default 7s) post-submit."

ConfirmationAudit {
  "Per fill, the audit task issues getTransaction(sig, commitment=Confirmed) with retry policy:"

  retries {
    attempt_1 = "no wait — first try"
    attempt_2 = "1s — retry after transient RPC error or null response"
    attempt_3 = "2s — retry"
    attempt_4 = "4s — last try"
  }

  transient = "RPC transport error (timeout, 429, 5xx) OR null response while tx age inside finality grace window (current slot − fill.submit_slot < 32). After 32 slots, null is treated as authoritative `missing`."

  on_rpc_exhaustion {
    "All 4 attempts fail with transport errors:"
    set_confirmed_at_ns_null = true
    set_fills_error          = "audit-rpc-failure"
    log                      = "warn with tx signature + last error"
    mutate_position_state    = false        // outcome unknown; operator inspects via replay <sig>
  }

  on_authoritative_outcome {
    fill_confirmed_ok       = "mark fills.confirmed_at_ns"
    fill_reverted_or_missing_past_grace {
      buy_case          = "position state := failed_reverted (no tokens transferred)"
      partial_sell_case = "roll back realised_frac and realised_sol; re-evaluate exits on next event"
      final_sell_case   = "position reopened with previous version's state"
    }
    position_acted_on_reverted_price_update = "On next Confirmed event for the mint, recompute peak and apply / no-op."
  }
}

## 2. Frame budget

"A `frame` = one inbound chain update."

FrameBudget {
  // step → (p99 budget, what runs)
  stream_next_wakeup {
    budget = "~50µs"
    what   = "tokio + gRPC client"
  }
  decode_tx_to_chain_event {
    budget = "<100µs"
    what   = "borsh / log parse"
  }
  open_positions_lookup {
    budget = "<1µs"
    what   = "DashMap"
  }
  pos_apply_and_evaluate_exits {
    budget = "<50µs"
    what   = "pure compute"
  }
  strategy_evaluate_buy {
    budget = "<50µs"
    what   = "pure compute"
  }
  tokio_spawn_execute {
    budget = "<10µs"
    what   = "task spawn"
  }
  frame_total = "< 500µs"
  off_frame_execute_buy_to_submitted = "p50 < 250ms, p99 < 1s (hits N1)"
}

## 3. Data model (DuckDB)

"DuckDB chosen per CLAUDE.md. Append-only."

```sql
CREATE TABLE chain_events (
    slot                 BIGINT      NOT NULL,
    received_at_ns       BIGINT      NOT NULL,
    block_time           BIGINT,
    dex_key              VARCHAR     NOT NULL,
    program_id           VARCHAR     NOT NULL,
    event_kind           VARCHAR     NOT NULL,    -- INIT|CREATE|MIGRATE|DEPOSIT|BUY|SELL
    tx_signature         VARCHAR     NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,
    signer               VARCHAR,
    base_mint            VARCHAR,
    quote_mint           VARCHAR,
    pool                 VARCHAR,
    sol_value            DOUBLE,
    base_reserve         DOUBLE,
    quote_reserve        DOUBLE,
    price_quote_per_base DOUBLE,
    confirmed            BOOLEAN     DEFAULT FALSE   -- set by confirmation_audit task
);
CREATE INDEX chain_events_mint_idx ON chain_events(base_mint);

CREATE TABLE signal_decisions (
    tx_signature        VARCHAR   NOT NULL,
    decided_at_ns       BIGINT    NOT NULL,
    ok                  BOOLEAN   NOT NULL,
    filters_passed      VARCHAR   NOT NULL,    -- JSON text; see note below
    filters_failed      VARCHAR   NOT NULL,    -- JSON text; see note below
    risk_reason         VARCHAR,                -- non-null if risk engine rejected
    PRIMARY KEY (tx_signature)
);

CREATE TABLE mint_enrichment (
    mint                       VARCHAR PRIMARY KEY,
    fetched_at                 TIMESTAMP NOT NULL,
    decimals                   INTEGER,
    supply                     DOUBLE,
    mint_authority             VARCHAR,
    freeze_authority           VARCHAR,
    top10_concentration        DOUBLE,
    holder_count               INTEGER,
    lp_burned_or_locked        BOOLEAN,
    deployer                   VARCHAR,
    deployer_prior_launches    INTEGER,
    notes                      VARCHAR        -- JSON text; see note below
);

CREATE TABLE positions (
    position_id        UUID       NOT NULL,
    version            INTEGER    NOT NULL,
    mode               VARCHAR    NOT NULL,             -- live | paper
    state              VARCHAR    NOT NULL,             -- opening | open | closing | closed | failed | failed_reverted
    mint               VARCHAR    NOT NULL,
    dex_key            VARCHAR    NOT NULL,
    pool               VARCHAR    NOT NULL,
    pool_signature     VARCHAR    NOT NULL,             -- entry-trigger tx
    entry_slot         BIGINT     NOT NULL,
    entry_at           TIMESTAMP  NOT NULL,
    entry_price        DOUBLE     NOT NULL,
    entry_sol_size     DOUBLE     NOT NULL,
    baseline_quote_reserve DOUBLE NOT NULL,
    token_amount_open  DOUBLE     NOT NULL,
    peak_price         DOUBLE     NOT NULL,
    realised_frac      DOUBLE     NOT NULL,
    realised_sol       DOUBLE     NOT NULL,
    pnl_sol            DOUBLE,
    pnl_pct            DOUBLE,
    exit_reason        VARCHAR,
    closed_at          TIMESTAMP,
    updated_at         TIMESTAMP  NOT NULL,
    notes              VARCHAR,                          -- JSON text; frozen insider_set + audit metadata
    PRIMARY KEY (position_id, version)
);
CREATE INDEX positions_state_idx    ON positions(state);
CREATE INDEX positions_mint_idx     ON positions(mint);

CREATE TABLE fills (
    fill_id           UUID       PRIMARY KEY,
    position_id       UUID       NOT NULL,
    side              VARCHAR    NOT NULL,              -- buy | sell
    reason            VARCHAR    NOT NULL,              -- entry|hard_stop|ladder|trailing_stop|liquidity_drain|insider_sell|decay|time_stop|shutdown
    requested_at_ns   BIGINT     NOT NULL,
    submitted_at_ns   BIGINT,
    confirmed_at_ns   BIGINT,
    tx_signature      VARCHAR,
    fraction_of_pos   DOUBLE     NOT NULL,
    tokens            DOUBLE     NOT NULL,
    quote_filled      DOUBLE     NOT NULL,
    fee_sol           DOUBLE     NOT NULL,
    slippage_bps      INTEGER,
    swqos_provider    VARCHAR,
    error             VARCHAR
);

CREATE TABLE blocklist (
    address    VARCHAR PRIMARY KEY,
    reason     VARCHAR,
    added_at   TIMESTAMP NOT NULL
);

CREATE VIEW open_positions AS
SELECT * FROM positions p
WHERE version = (SELECT MAX(version) FROM positions WHERE position_id = p.position_id)
  AND state IN ('opening','open','closing');
```

"JSON-like columns (signal_decisions.filters_passed/failed, mint_enrichment.notes, positions.notes) are stored as VARCHAR containing JSON text and parsed in Rust via serde_json."
"DuckDB's JSON column type triggers an extension autoload that requires network access — incompatible with the SPEC §N4 single-binary footprint. See docs/diary.md Decision-0005."

"daily_pnl is intentionally NOT a SQL view. The bundled DuckDB build ships without ICU, so date/time scalar functions (today(), current_date, current_timestamp) are not in the catalog. stats.rs (§12) computes today's UTC midnight in Rust and runs the equivalent query with a TIMESTAMP-typed parameter:"

```sql
SELECT SUM(pnl_sol) FILTER (WHERE state = 'closed' AND closed_at >= ?)
FROM positions;
```

## 4. Exit detection

### 4.1 Two clocks

TwoClocks {
  EventClock_primary {
    "Every BUY/SELL on a mint we own runs through the hot loop."
    "pos.apply(&evt) updates price/peak/reserves; each SellTrigger is evaluated in priority order; first to fire wins."
  }

  WallClockHeartbeat_safety_net {
    interval = "configurable, default 100ms"
    "Iterates open_positions; fires only time_stop and decay when N samples haven't arrived event-driven."
  }
}

### 4.2 Concurrent-fill semantics

ConcurrentFill {
  dispatch = "When a sell tx is dispatched: state := closing in memory, pending_sell: AtomicBool := true. Subsequent triggers of equal-or-lower priority ignored until the pending tx resolves."
  preempt  = "A higher-priority trigger preempts: new sell tx dispatched with a higher compute-unit price (multiplier in config) so it lands first. Solana doesn't truly cancel txs — racing-with-fee is the only mechanism."
  on_confirmed_prior_tx = "Advance realised_frac and realised_sol, clear pending_sell, re-evaluate exits."
  on_confirmed_failure  = "Clear pending_sell, re-evaluate."
}

### 4.3 Slot-level price collisions

SlotCollisions {
  "pos.apply(&evt) records (slot, signature) of the latest applied event."
  out_of_order = "A later-arriving event with evt.slot < last_applied.slot is dropped."
  same_slot_diff_sig = "Applied if (slot, signature) hash-sorts after the last (deterministic tiebreak)."
}

### 4.4 Insider set construction

"The insider_sell SellTrigger needs a per-position set of addresses that count as `insiders`."
"Set captured ONCE at entry (frozen for lifetime) so the hot path checks signer ∈ set in O(1) without RPC."

InsiderSet {
  members = [
    "pool_event.signer — address that submitted the INIT/CREATE/MIGRATE/DEPOSIT tx that triggered entry",
    "deployer (mint_enrichment.deployer) if different from #1",
    "top-N initial holders captured during entry-burst enrichment"
  ]

  topN_config {
    N            = "[strategy.buy_trigger].insider_capture_top_n (default 5)"
    min_pct      = "[strategy.buy_trigger].insider_capture_min_pct (default 0.01 = 1%)"
    source       = "getTokenLargestAccounts snapshot at entry slot"
    filter_out   = ["pool's own ATA", "bot's ATA", "WSOL mint", "holders < min_pct"]
  }

  storage = "Lives on in-memory Position as insider_set: HashSet<Pubkey> (typically ≤7 entries). Also persisted as JSON in positions.notes at v1 (replay / audit reconstruction)."
}

"Trigger evaluation (hot path, on every BUY/SELL event for the mint):"

```rust
if matches!(evt.event_kind, SELL)
   && pos.insider_set.contains(&evt.signer)
   && (evt.tokens_sold / enrich.supply) >= trigger.insider_pct {
    fire(SellReason::InsiderSell);
}
```

"If the entry-burst enrichment for largest-accounts times out: set = {signer, deployer} only; logged."
"Bot does NOT block entry on the largest-accounts query — BuyTrigger has its own enrichment dependencies; this snapshot runs in parallel."

## 5. Crate / module inventory

```
liquid-snipe-rs/                  # sibling to liquid-snipe/
  Cargo.toml                      # workspace
  config.toml.example
  crates/
    liquid-snipe/                 # bin: hot loop owner, CLI, app wiring
    liquid-snipe-core/            # types, config, DuckDB, risk engine, slippage controller
    liquid-snipe-stream/          # gRPC + WS subscriptions; decoders
    liquid-snipe-strategy/        # BuyTrigger + SellTriggers + heartbeat evaluators
    liquid-snipe-simulator/       # paper-mode fill model
    liquid-snipe-exec/            # sol-trade-sdk wrapper for buy/sell
```

### 5.1 liquid-snipe (bin)

Bin_liquid_snipe {
  main_rs                   = "runtime bootstrap, install crypto provider, parse CLI"
  cli_rs                    = "clap subcommands: run (default), replay <sig>, stats, migrate"
  app_rs                    = "wires AppState + shared atomics; spawns background tasks; OWNS the hot loop"
  hot_loop_rs               = "async fn run(stream, state, strategy) -> !"
  bg_blockhash_rs           = "refresher task"
  bg_wallet_balance_rs      = "polls getBalance (+ WSOL ATA) on [wallet].balance_refresh_ms; updates AtomicU64; recomputes bankroll"
  bg_enrichment_rs          = "speculative mint fetcher"
  bg_heartbeat_rs           = "wall-clock tick: time_stop, decay fallback"
  bg_housekeeping_rs        = "prune closed positions, expire enrichment"
  bg_persistence_rs         = "drains crossbeam::channel<DbWrite> → DuckDB batched inserts"
  bg_confirmation_audit_rs  = "re-check fills at Confirmed; handle reverts"
  bg_slippage_controller_rs = "tracks consecutive-failure window, bumps slippage_bps atomic"
  bg_config_reloader_rs     = "SIGHUP handler → reload TOML, swap source/SWQOS/strategy"
  metrics_rs                = "structured logs, frame timing histogram"
  stats_rs                  = "stats subcommand output (text + JSON)"
}

### 5.2 liquid-snipe-core

Crate_core {
  types_rs    = "ChainEvent, EventKind, Position, Fill, EnrichedMint, DexKey"
  dexes_rs    = "DEX registry: program IDs, event kinds, decoder selector"
  config_rs   = "TOML loader, {{helius}} expansion, validation, Config::reload(path)"
  wallet_rs   = "wallet loader (file path or WALLET_BASE58_ENV); fatal on missing in live"
  db_rs       = "DuckDB connection, migrations, prepared statements"
  risk_rs     = "RiskEngine::pre_entry_ok(plan, snapshot) -> Result<(), RejectReason>; bankroll-relative thresholds"
  slippage_rs = "controller state struct: failure window, current bps, bump policy"
  state_rs    = "AppState; DashMap<Pubkey, Position>, DashMap<Pubkey, EnrichedMint>"
  consts_rs   = "WSOL, burn addresses"
}

### 5.3 liquid-snipe-stream

Crate_stream {
  source_rs      = "enum Source { Yellowstone, HeliusWs, Replay } → Stream<Item = RawTx>; Source::reload(new_config) swaps endpoint"
  yellowstone_rs = "YellowstoneSource over yellowstone-grpc-client. Auto-reconnect with backoff."
  helius_ws_rs   = "fallback path"
  replay_rs      = "reads recorded JSONL of past events for offline test runs"
  decoders_rs    = "per-DEX decode(raw_tx) -> Option<ChainEvent>. Anchor decoders via carbon-*-decoder. Legacy log-substring fallback for Raydium AMM v4 (initialize2, ray_log) and pump.fun snake_case discriminators."
  parser_rs      = "extract (base_mint, quote_mint, base_reserve, quote_reserve, price) from decoded tx"
}

### 5.4 liquid-snipe-strategy

Crate_strategy {
  buy_trigger_rs   = "BuyTrigger { filters: Vec<Filter> } ⇒ evaluate(event, enrich, risk) -> BuyDecision"
  filters_rs       = "enum Filter { EventKind, MinSolLiquidity, DexAllowlist, QuoteMints, RenouncedAuthorities, LpBurned, MaxTop10Concentration, MinHolderCount, MaxMarketCapSol, DeployerMaxPriorLaunches, DeployerBlocklist } — pure fns"
  sell_triggers_rs = "enum SellTrigger { HardStop, Ladder, TrailingStop, LiquidityDrain, Decay, InsiderSell, TimeStop } — priority + evaluator"
  evaluator_rs     = "Strategy::evaluate_buy and Strategy::evaluate_exits; stable priority order"
  decay_ring_rs    = "small in-memory ring of last N price samples per position, used by Decay"
}

### 5.5 liquid-snipe-simulator

Crate_simulator {
  fill_rs  = "linear-impact slippage model + flat gas (configurable defaults)"
  paper_rs = "when mode=paper, liquid-snipe-exec routes here; same Fill shape as live"
}

### 5.6 liquid-snipe-exec

Crate_exec {
  client_rs     = "ExecClient holds Arc<TradingInfrastructure> (sol-trade-sdk Method 2: Shared infrastructure) + Arc<Keypair>"
  swqos_rs      = "builds Vec<SwqosConfig> from [[swqos]] config array — supports default RPC, Jito, Temporal/Nozomi (hosted or self-hosted via custom URL), ZeroSlot, FlashBlock, BlockRazor, Astralane, NextBlock, SpeedLanding"
  dex_params_rs = "per-DEX TradeBuyParams / TradeSellParams builders. PumpFun/PumpSwap use decoded ChainEvent.execution_hint first, then PoolCache, then RPC fallback. Raydium AMM v4 / CPMM and Meteora DAMM v2 use from_pool_address_by_rpc (prefetched by enrichment)."
  buy_rs        = "async fn buy(plan, blockhash, slippage_bps, gas) -> Result<Fill>"
  sell_rs       = "async fn sell(pos, fraction, reason, blockhash, slippage_bps, gas) -> Result<Fill>"
  wsol_wrap_rs  = "helper: wrap N SOL → WSOL ATA. Exposed as `liquid-snipe wrap-sol <amount>` subcommand. Runs once at boot if [wallet].auto_wrap_sol > 0."
}

### 5.7 DEX → sol-trade-sdk::DexType mapping

DexMapping {
  pumpfun_kv {
    dex_type       = "PumpFun"
    params_builder = "PumpFunParams::from_trade / from_dev_trade (event-derived from decoded execution hints)"
  }
  pumpswap_kv {
    dex_type       = "PumpSwap"
    params_builder = "PumpSwapParams::from_trade (event-derived from decoded execution hints)"
  }
  raydium_amm_kv {
    dex_type       = "RaydiumAmmV4"
    params_builder = "RaydiumAmmV4Params::from_pool_address_by_rpc (prefetch)"
  }
  raydium_cpmm_kv {
    dex_type       = "RaydiumCpmm"
    params_builder = "RaydiumCpmmParams::from_pool_address_by_rpc (prefetch)"
  }
  meteora_damm_v2_kv {
    dex_type       = "MeteoraDammV2"
    params_builder = "MeteoraDammV2Params::from_pool_address_by_rpc (prefetch)"
  }
  capture_only_dexes {
    dexes    = ["raydium-clmm", "meteora-dlmm", "orca-whirlpool"]
    dex_type = "(no SDK support)"
    note     = "capture & evaluate only; execution skipped with `signal:fired,exec:unsupported`"
  }
}

## 6. Config schema

"TOML. Every tuning value is configurable. Defaults conservative; operator overrides for prod."

```toml
[mode]
default = "live"   # live | paper | observe; CLI flag wins

[wallet]
keypair_path       = "data/wallet.json"  # OR set WALLET_BASE58_ENV
keypair_env        = "WALLET_BASE58"
auto_wrap_sol      = 0.0                 # SOL→WSOL on boot, 0 = no wrap
balance_refresh_ms = 1000                # background poll; independent of [blockhash].refresh_ms

[risk]
# All percentages are of bankroll. Bankroll =
#   wallet.lamports/1e9 + WSOL_ATA.balance + Σ open_positions.realised_sol
#     (closed-rung proceeds from partial sells not yet redeployed)
# Unrealised mark-to-market is NOT bankroll — tracked separately as
#   "open exposure" against max_total_risk_pct.
# Recomputed on boot and every fill.
max_total_risk_pct      = 50    # halt new entries while open exposure > 50%
max_per_trade_risk_pct  = 5     # size each new trade as 5% of bankroll
max_daily_loss_pct      = 10    # halt new entries on -10% day
max_open_positions      = 4
min_wallet_sol_floor    = 0.05  # absolute SOL floor

[slippage]
default_bps        = 300        # 3% start
max_bps            = 2500       # cap (25%)
bump_bps           = 1000       # +10% per bump
fail_window_n      = 5          # consec failures before bump
fail_window_secs   = 60         # failures only count within window
reset_on_success   = true

# --- Streaming source (hot-swappable on SIGHUP) ---
[grpc]
enabled        = true
endpoint       = "https://your-yellowstone.example.com:443"
auth_token_env = "GRPC_AUTH_TOKEN"

[grpc.fallback_ws]               # used when gRPC unavailable
enabled      = true
http_url     = "{{helius}}"
ws_url       = "{{helius}}"
max_inflight = 32                # bounded getTransaction concurrency

[rpc]
http_url         = "{{helius}}"  # enrichment + blockhash + sol-trade-sdk
commitment_hot   = "processed"
commitment_audit = "confirmed"

# --- SWQOS (hot-swappable on SIGHUP) ---
# Each entry maps 1:1 to sol-trade-sdk SwqosConfig variant.
# Provide either `region` (hosted) or `url` (custom / self-hosted).
[mev]
mev_protection = false           # global flag (Astralane QUIC :9000 / BlockRazor)

[[swqos]]
provider = "default"             # plain RPC submission
url      = "{{rpc.http_url}}"

# [[swqos]] provider = "jito";        uuid = "...";          region = "Frankfurt"
# [[swqos]] provider = "temporal";    api_token_env = "TEMPORAL_API_TOKEN"; region = "Frankfurt"
# [[swqos]] provider = "temporal";    api_token_env = "TEMPORAL_API_TOKEN"; url = "http://my-relay:8080"
# [[swqos]] provider = "zeroslot";    api_token_env = "ZEROSLOT_API_TOKEN"; region = "Frankfurt"
# [[swqos]] provider = "flashblock";  api_token_env = "FLASHBLOCK_TOKEN";   region = "Frankfurt"
# [[swqos]] provider = "blockrazor";  api_token_env = "BLOCKRAZOR_TOKEN";   region = "Frankfurt"
# [[swqos]] provider = "astralane";   api_token_env = "ASTRALANE_KEY";      region = "Frankfurt"; transport = "quic"
# [[swqos]] provider = "nextblock";   api_token_env = "NEXTBLOCK_TOKEN";    region = "NewYork"
# [[swqos]] provider = "speedlanding"; api_token_env = "SPEEDLANDING_TOKEN"; region = "Frankfurt"

[gas]
compute_unit_limit       = 500_000
compute_unit_price_micro = 150_000
priority_fee_sol_buy     = 0.001
priority_fee_sol_sell    = 0.001
preempt_fee_multiplier   = 2.0   # multiplier when higher-priority sell preempts pending one

[dexes]
enabled = [
  "raydium-amm","raydium-cpmm","raydium-clmm",
  "orca-whirlpool","meteora-dlmm","meteora-damm-v2",
  "pumpfun","pumpswap",
]

# --- Tuning (all configurable) ---
[hot_loop]
frame_warn_us = 1000             # log if a frame exceeds this
spawn_buffer  = 8                # bounded executor concurrency

[blockhash]
refresh_ms = 400

[enrichment]
mint_ttl_sec        = 300
deployer_ttl_sec    = 3600
deployer_lookback   = 50
required_timeout_ms = 800        # how long to hold a candidate waiting

[heartbeat]
tick_ms = 250                    # wall-clock cadence for time/decay fallback

[housekeeping]
tick_sec = 30

[persistence]
batch_max_rows = 256
batch_max_ms   = 1000
duckdb_path    = "data/liquid-snipe.duckdb"

[confirmation_audit]
delay_ms = 7000                  # wait this long after submit before re-checking at Confirmed

# --- Strategy ---
[strategy]
id = "default"

[strategy.buy_trigger]
event_kinds                    = ["INIT", "MIGRATE"]
min_sol_liquidity              = 10.0
dex_allowlist                  = []          # empty = use [dexes].enabled
quote_mints                    = ["WSOL"]
require_renounced_authorities  = true
require_lp_burned              = false
max_top10_holder_concentration = 0.50
min_holder_count               = 0
max_market_cap_sol             = 0           # 0 = no cap
deployer_max_prior_launches    = 0           # 0 = first-time; null = no limit
deployer_blocklist_path        = "data/blocklist.json"
enrichment_timeout_ms          = 800

# Insider-set capture (insider_sell SellTrigger; §4.4). Snapshot at entry, frozen.
insider_capture_top_n          = 5           # top-N largest holders to include
insider_capture_min_pct        = 0.01        # exclude holders below this fraction of supply

# Sell triggers — array order serves as tiebreaker on equal SPEC priority.
[[strategy.sell_triggers]]
kind     = "hard_stop"
stop_pct = -0.15

[[strategy.sell_triggers]]
kind  = "ladder"
rungs = [
  { profit = 0.10, sell = 0.50 },
  { profit = 0.25, sell = 0.25 },
  { profit = 0.50, sell = 0.25 },
]

[[strategy.sell_triggers]]
kind      = "trailing_stop"
trail_pct = 0.08

[[strategy.sell_triggers]]
kind      = "liquidity_drain"
drain_pct = 0.5

[[strategy.sell_triggers]]
kind        = "insider_sell"
insider_pct = 0.10

[[strategy.sell_triggers]]
kind      = "decay"
samples_n = 4

[[strategy.sell_triggers]]
kind     = "time_stop"
hold_sec = 300

[logging]
level  = "info"
format = "json"
```

### 6.1 Validation

ConfigValidation {
  boot = [
    "at least one filter on the BuyTrigger",
    "at least one SellTrigger",
    "max_per_trade_risk_pct ≤ max_total_risk_pct",
    "min_wallet_sol_floor > 0 in live mode",
    "wallet keypair resolvable in live mode"
  ]
  helius_expansion = "{{helius}} ⇒ https://mainnet.helius-rpc.com/?api-key=$HELIUS_API_KEY"
  empty_swqos_list = "fatal error in live mode"
}

## 7. Adaptive slippage controller

"State in liquid-snipe-core::slippage::Controller:"

```rust
struct Controller {
    base_bps:         u16,                // from config
    current_bps:      AtomicU16,          // read by execute_buy
    max_bps:          u16,
    bump_bps:         u16,
    failures:         Mutex<VecDeque<Instant>>,
    fail_window:      Duration,
    fail_threshold:   usize,
    reset_on_success: bool,
}
```

SlippageBehaviour {
  every_buy_attempt = "executor reads current_bps ⇒ slippage_basis_points in TradeBuyParams"
  on_failure        = "call record_failure(now). Drop entries older than fail_window. If remaining ≥ fail_threshold: current_bps = min(current_bps + bump_bps, max_bps); clear failure deque."
  on_success        = "If reset_on_success: clear deque; if current_bps > base_bps, decay one step toward base."
  logging           = "All transitions logged structurally; persisted to signal_decisions.risk_reason for audit."
}

## 8. Hot-reload mechanism

"bg/config_reloader.rs registers a SIGHUP handler."

ReloadFlow {
  step_1 = "Re-parse config.toml. Validate."
  step_2 = "Compute diff: which sub-trees changed."

  step_3_dispatch {
    grpc_or_dexes      = "[grpc], [grpc.fallback_ws], [dexes] → Source::reload(new) (drops stream, reopens, in-flight drains)"
    swqos_or_mev       = "[[swqos]], [mev] → rebuild Vec<SwqosConfig>; ask liquid-snipe-exec to swap (TradingInfrastructure rebuilt; in-flight buys/sells use old until done)"
    slippage           = "[slippage] → Controller::update(new)"
    runtime_globals    = "[gas], [hot_loop], [heartbeat], [persistence] → atomic swap of relevant struct"
    strategy_or_risk   = "[strategy] and [risk] → swap Arc<Strategy> and Arc<RiskProfile> in AppState. In-flight positions retain a snapshot of their original SellTriggers (cloned at entry). New entries see new strategy. Logged."
  }

  step_4 = "Emit a structured log line per changed sub-tree."

  failures = "Validation error / gRPC reconnect failure ⇒ leave old config in place; log error."
}

InFlightSemantics {
  rule = "Clone-at-entry is total: every in-flight Position carries an Arc<StrategySnapshot> taken when opened; hot loop evaluates exits against snapshot, NOT current AppState.strategy."

  // reload change → (applies to in-flight?, applies to new?)
  selltrigger_param_changed      = "in_flight: no, new: yes"
  selltrigger_removed            = "in_flight: no, new: yes"
  selltrigger_kind_added         = "in_flight: no, new: yes"
  risk_thresholds_changed        = "in_flight: yes for next entry's risk check; sizing already locked. new: yes."
  buy_trigger_changed            = "in_flight: n/a (past entry). new: yes."
  slippage_changed               = "in_flight: yes (global, not per-position). new: yes."
  gas_hot_loop_heartbeat_changed = "in_flight: yes (runtime-global). new: yes."
  grpc_swqos_changed             = "in_flight: yes (substrate, not per-position). new: yes."

  operator_retroactive_upgrade {
    "Close & reopen. Either (a) `liquid-snipe close <position_id> --reason manual` (planned subcommand), or (b) wait for existing triggers to fire naturally."
    "NO mid-flight trigger upgrade — would invalidate priority ordering AND the pending_sell state machine."
  }
}

"On every reload mutating [strategy] or [risk], reloader emits:"

```
config-reload: strategy swapped (id=v3 → v4). Diff:
  added:    insider_sell { insider_pct=0.05 }
  modified: trailing_stop { trail_pct: 0.08 → 0.06 }
  removed:  none
in-flight positions retained original strategy: 3
  - position a3w… (entry +12s)   strategy=v3
  - position 7tj… (entry +4s)    strategy=v3
  - position f9q… (entry +1s)    strategy=v3
new positions opened from now will use strategy v4
```

## 9. Workspace dependencies

```toml
[workspace.dependencies]
liquid-snipe           = { path = "crates/liquid-snipe" }
liquid-snipe-core      = { path = "crates/liquid-snipe-core" }
liquid-snipe-stream    = { path = "crates/liquid-snipe-stream" }
liquid-snipe-strategy  = { path = "crates/liquid-snipe-strategy" }
liquid-snipe-simulator = { path = "crates/liquid-snipe-simulator" }
liquid-snipe-exec      = { path = "crates/liquid-snipe-exec" }

# Solana / trading
sol-trade-sdk  = { path = "../../reference/sol-trade-sdk", version = "4.0.8" }
solana-sdk     = "3.0"
solana-client  = "3.1"
solana-program = "3.0"

# Carbon decoders only (no Pipeline)
carbon-core                    = "0.12"
carbon-raydium-amm-v4-decoder  = "0.12"
carbon-raydium-cpmm-decoder    = "0.12"
carbon-raydium-clmm-decoder    = "0.12"
carbon-orca-whirlpool-decoder  = "0.12"
carbon-meteora-dlmm-decoder    = "0.12"
carbon-meteora-damm-v2-decoder = "0.12"
carbon-pumpfun-decoder         = "0.12"
carbon-pump-swap-decoder       = "0.12"

yellowstone-grpc-client = "5"
yellowstone-grpc-proto  = "5"
duckdb = { version = "1", features = ["bundled"] }

tokio       = { version = "1", features = ["full"] }
tokio-util  = { version = "0.7", features = ["rt"] }
futures     = "0.3"
borsh       = { version = "1", features = ["derive"] }

# Hot-loop primitives
dashmap           = "6"
arc-swap          = "1"
crossbeam-channel = "0.5"
parking_lot       = "0.12"

# Config reload
notify            = "6"            # optional file watcher in addition to SIGHUP
signal-hook-tokio = "0.3"

clap               = { version = "4", features = ["derive"] }
serde              = { version = "1", features = ["derive"] }
toml               = "0.8"
tracing            = "0.1"
tracing-subscriber = { version = "0.3", features = ["env-filter","json"] }
dotenvy            = "0.15"
clru               = "0.6"
anyhow             = "1"
thiserror          = "1"
uuid               = { version = "1", features = ["v4","serde"] }
chrono             = "0.4"
```

"Excluded: carbon-yellowstone-grpc-datasource, carbon-core::Pipeline (multi-stage shape rejected). Carbon decoders only."

## 10. Tests

Tests {
  unit_property {
    crate = "liquid-snipe-strategy"
    cases = [
      "Filter pure-fn tests with synthetic ChainEvent + EnrichedMint fixtures (in-test, no external files)",
      "SellTrigger priority: construct Position + ChainEvent satisfying multiple triggers; assert highest-priority fires",
      "Concurrent-fill: simulate pending_sell true + new higher-priority trigger ⇒ asserts preempt sell dispatched with multiplied fee",
      "Decay ring: rolling-window correctness"
    ]
  }

  frame_budget_regression {
    crate = "liquid-snipe"
    "Replay 10_000 synthetic gRPC updates through hot_loop::run with all backgrounds stubbed."
    assertions = ["p99 < 500µs", "p99.9 < 1ms"]
    gate       = "CI (AC2)"
  }

  integration_paper_round_trip {
    crate = "liquid-snipe"
    "Spin Source::Replay of recorded chain events; run full app in paper; assert known fixture produces known set of positions and fills rows."
  }

  integration_hot_reload {
    crate = "liquid-snipe"
    "Boot config A; SIGHUP after switching to config B (different SellTrigger threshold + SWQOS list)."
    assertions = ["gRPC reconnect happened", "slippage controller picked up new params", "in-flight position kept its old triggers"]
  }

  integration_live_test_wallet {
    runner = "manual (operator)"
    "Per AC4. Documented in docs/manual-tests.md."
  }
}

## 11. Operational notes

OperationalNotes {
  wallet_provisioning {
    "Operator generates data/wallet.json (`solana-keygen new -o data/wallet.json`) or sets WALLET_BASE58_ENV, then funds it."
    "Bot does NOT generate one."
    "Boot fails fast in live on missing/invalid wallet, with a clear message."
  }

  wrapping_sol {
    "First WSOL pair needs a WSOL ATA."
    "Run `liquid-snipe wrap-sol <amount>` once, or set [wallet].auto_wrap_sol to wrap on every boot."
  }

  first_run_migration {
    "`liquid-snipe migrate` creates the DuckDB schema. Idempotent. Policy in §11.1."
  }

  secrets {
    "HELIUS_API_KEY, GRPC_AUTH_TOKEN, all SWQOS API tokens loaded via env (dotenvy reads .env.local). Never logged."
  }

  shutdown {
    "SIGINT → CancellationToken → drop stream → drain workers → final SELL on every open position (reason = shutdown) → persistence drains → exit."
    budget = "30s; force-exit on timeout"
  }

  hot_swap = "SIGHUP triggers config reload (§8)."

  replay = "`liquid-snipe replay <tx_signature>` reconstructs the decision trail from chain_events, signal_decisions, positions, fills. Output spec in §13."
}

### 11.1 Migration / schema evolution

"DuckDB schema versioned via a _meta table:"

```sql
CREATE TABLE _meta (
    key      VARCHAR PRIMARY KEY,
    value    VARCHAR
);
-- _meta rows include:
--   schema_version → integer monotonically increasing
--   created_at     → ISO-8601 timestamp of first migrate
--   binary_version → semver of the liquid-snipe build that last opened the DB
```

MigrationFiles {
  location  = "crates/liquid-snipe-core/migrations/V<n>__<name>.sql"
  examples  = ["V1__initial.sql", "V2__add_position_notes.sql"]
  embedding = "include_str! at compile time"
  immutability = "Filenames are immutable once released; new schema deltas always get a higher V<n>."
}

MigrateBehaviour {
  step_1 = "Open the DuckDB file (create if missing)."
  step_2 = "Read _meta.schema_version (missing ⇒ 0)."
  step_3 = "Read the binary's EXPECTED_SCHEMA_VERSION constant."

  step_4_branch {
    db_eq_binary = "no-op, exit 0 (idempotent — safe to run repeatedly)"
    db_lt_binary = "Apply each V<n>__*.sql for n in (db+1..=binary) inside a single transaction per file; bump _meta.schema_version after each successful file."
    db_gt_binary = "FATAL. Print: `error: DB at schema_version=N, this binary expects M (M < N). Refusing to open. Use a newer binary.` Exit 2. Do not open the DB."
  }
}

ForwardOnly {
  "Migrations are append-only."
  allowed     = ["CREATE TABLE", "ALTER TABLE … ADD COLUMN", "CREATE INDEX", "CREATE VIEW", "INSERT seed data"]
  not_allowed = "drop columns, drop tables, or rewrite existing rows in a way that loses information unless operator passes --force-destructive"
  intent      = "data/liquid-snipe.duckdb is a permanent record of the bot's history; schema evolves additively."
}

BootCheck {
  "Every non-migrate subcommand opens DB read/write and verifies _meta.schema_version == EXPECTED_SCHEMA_VERSION."
  lower      = "Boot fails fast: `error: DB schema is outdated. Run liquid-snipe migrate and retry.`"
  higher     = "Fatal as above."
  auto_migrate_on_boot = false   // schema changes are operator-acknowledged
}

